Am Mittwoch, 5. Oktober 2005 07:54 schrieb Joerg Platte:
Hi!

> Kernels starting with 2.6.13 detect a HyperThreading CPU two times as C=
PU0:
> ACPI: CPU0 (power states: C1[C1])
> ACPI: CPU0 (power states: C1[C1])
>
> Then, the kernel hangs. Previous kernels did not have this problem. The
> dsdt is attached.

The problem exist on various Fujitsu-Siemens computers (W600 series). Ker=
nels=20
up to 2.6.12 can boot without ACPI related problems. All tested  newer=20
kernels (2.6.13, 2.6.13.3 and 2.6.14-rc3) hang after ACPI cpu detection. =
I=20
attached the /proc/acpi/dsdt output to this mail. What can I do to resolv=
e=20
this issue? I solved this problem temporaly by disabling hypter threading=
 in=20
BIOS, but there should be a better solution...

regards,
J=F6rg

